li","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-7e[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]🧱 BLOCKS lines: show on every prerequisite what waits on it[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every open task that other open tasks depend on carries one [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]machine-owned `🧱 **BLOCKS:**` child line that mirrors its [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]dependents' Depends-On links. The line is kept exact by `bob task [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]reconcile`, updated immediately by every dependency writer [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](Ctrl+Shift+P, chip ×, hand edits and undo, capture `&`, capture [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]dependency drops), rendered in Obsidian as chips that show what [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]finishing the task would free, and never read back as dependency [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]input.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]prerequisite_blocks_lines.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/prerequisite_blocks_lines.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-7e[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-7e/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The BLOCKS-line contract, managed-line registry, and vectors[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: write docs/task-dependencies.md §14 (grammar, membership, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]minting, order, position, authority, writers, gestures, chips, kill [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]switch, outputs), grow §2.4 into the managed-child-line registry, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the BK/BR/BW/BC/MC vectors, and align projects.md, capture.md, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]getting-started.md.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust grammar, shared planner, guards, projects-sync anchor, [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]and config[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-core: add task_dependencies::blocks (parser, formatter, canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sort, slot, and the one shared line planner), guard every Rust Task Link[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and tree-close scanner against both managed dependency lines, anchor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Sub-projects after BLOCKS, and load dependencies.blocks_lines.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Recognisers and gesture guards in nav, cycler, and [/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]block-id-prompt[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-guards[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-guards: teach bob-navigation-hotkeys, task-status-cycler, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]block-id-prompt to recognise and ignore BLOCKS lines (Pomodoro scanners,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strike/restore, tree close, conversion, the hand-edit mirror) and route [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]or refuse gestures on them, then deploy on this host.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-ledger-tools BLOCKS chips with the 🔑 last-blocker badge[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chips[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chips: render BLOCKS lines in Live Preview and Reading view from a live [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reverse index of the Tasks memo, with the 🔑 badge, `frees N` summaries,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]past-tense frozen rows, and stale-entry styling; guard the plan-budget [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]link counter; deploy on this host.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob task reconcile owns the BLOCKS projection[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-reconcile[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-core, plugin-guards, chips[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-reconcile: export the accepted explicit edges from R1–R10, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]BLOCKS pass (mint, insert, rewrite, canonicalise, deduplicate, delete, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]warn, never prune on uncertainty, honour the kill switch), report it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]additively, and dry-run it against the live vault.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture `&` and dependency drops keep the mirror current[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-capture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-core, cli-reconcile[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-capture: stage each added prerequisite's BLOCKS entry (and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dependent's minted id) in the same capture batch, remove entries on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dependency drops, report rows additively, and keep Bob Mac Capture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]working without Swift changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Nav planner seam, minting, and cross-note follow-ups[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-writer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plugin-guards, cli-reconcile[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-writer: add the JS twin of the shared planner and the SB mint, make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planDependencyEdit emit same-note BLOCKS edits plus cross-note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-ups, add the preimage-checked follow-up writer, and wire the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared writer and the single same-note path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Every remaining nav writer, the hand-edit mirror, and undo[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-paths[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-writer[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-paths: route counted, marked, and batch Depends-On writers, counted [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Ctrl+D, the hand-edit mirror (including undo), project conversion, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Ctrl+Shift+M through the BLOCKS seam, with a test for every path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Install, verify, reach the MacBook, record[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-capture, nav-paths[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollout: install bob on this host, review the live dry-run, verify the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pilot script on a vault copy, sync plugins, update the MacBook on a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]best-effort basis, apply the accepted memory decisions, and record [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-ups.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-7e","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-7e.1","reasoning_effort":"high","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"bob-cli-7e.1"},"source_run_id":"run-c822f840656f14a6f64cf3b8c46e4ac9","started_at":"2026-10-13T15:12:03.266663+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.1","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.2","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.3","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.4","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.5","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.6","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.7","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.8","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.9","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-7e.land"]}
